{title: Ask God}
{subtitle: James 1:5}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | [F7sus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Con[Bb]sider it nothing but [Eb]joy, my brothers
[Gm7]When trials of every [Eb]kind come your way
[Bb]Testing of your faith produ[Eb]ces endurance
[Gm]Let it finish its work [Fsus4]today
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]So that [Eb]you may be mature and com[Bb]plete
Lacking [Eb]nothing in the [Gm]heart
If you lack [Eb]wisdom, do not [Gm]fear
Just turn to where the [Fsus4]light is [F]start
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask [Bb]God, who gives [F]generously [Gm]to [Eb]all
With[Bb]out find[F]ing fault, He [Gm]will [Eb]not fail
It will [Bb]be giv[F]en to him, it will [Gm]be giv[Eb]en to him
Ask in faith, [F7sus4]keep your heart from [Bb]strife [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But let him [Bb]ask in faith, without [Eb]doubting
For [Gm]the one who doubts [Eb]is like a wave
[Bb]Driven and tossed by the [Eb]wind
Unstable [Gm]in all he does and [F]saves
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask [Bb]God, who gives [F]generously [Gm]to [Eb]all
With[Bb]out find[F]ing fault, He [Gm]will [Eb]not fail
It will [Bb]be given to [F]him, it will [Gm]be giv[Eb]en to him
Ask in faith, [F7sus4]keep your heart from [Bb]strife
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Such a [Eb]person should not expect [F]to receive anyt[Bb]hing
From [Eb]the Lord, for dou-ble-[F]mind-ed minds are blind
Do not [Gm]be tossed about by the [Eb]wind
Stand firm in the truth you will [F]find
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Ask [Bb]God, who gives [F]generously [Gm]to [Eb]all
With[Bb]out find[F]ing fault, He [Gm]will [Eb]not fail
It will [Bb]be given to [F]him, it will [Gm]be giv[Eb]en to him
Ask in faith, [F7sus4]keep your heart from [Bb]strife [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
It will be [Bb]given to [F]him [Gm]
[Eb]Ask [Bb][F]God, and be [Bb]still
{end_of_verse}
